, "labels": ["o"], "number": "5'", "atf": "aš-bu-ma ik-ka-lu kar-ṣi | ut-ta-[(az)-za-mu]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: (Then) they convened and began to complain (and) grumble:"}, {"number": "6'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n tupšikku(m)-ma | iddūknâši || kabit | dull[u]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "6'", "atf": "tup-ši-ik-ku-ma GAZ-na-ši ka-bit# du-ul#-l[u*]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: “The toil indeed is killing us, hard is the work,"}, {"number": "7'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n <m>ād | šapšaqni", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "7'", "atf": "<ma>-a-ad# šap-ša#-aq-ni", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Too much our distress!"}, {"number": "8'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n alkāni | guzalâni | i ninēram-ma!", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "8'", "atf": "al-ka-ni {giš}gu-za-la-ni i ni-<ne₂>-ri-am-ma", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Come, let us slay our steward, …"}, {"number": "9'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n u kabta | dullani || i nišbir | nīr[ni]\n#note: @bib{RN59aa@170, 173} restore @akk{i ni-iš-h[u?-uṭ]} from the verb @i{šahāṭu} “to cast off”. On the “sandwiching” of the verb between two accusatives, a well-attested device in Babylonian literature, see the remarks in @bib{marquezrowe2016middle@62}.", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "9'", "atf": "u₃ ka-ab-ta du-ul-la-ni i-ni-iš-bir₅ ni-ir-[ni]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: and break our heavy work, our yoke!’"}, {"number": "10'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n (w)ê | ša īšû || ilu | ṭēma\n#note: On the name “(W)ê” of the god leader of the rebellion, previously interpreted by most scholars as Wê-ila or Aw-ila, see the commentary on this line in @bib{marquezrowe2016middle@62} (following @bib{krebernik2002geschlachtet@290}).  @bib{RN59aa@173-74} read @akk{UN} at the beginning. The epithet @i{ša išû ilu ṭēma} displays the same word order as in OB II 103, which shows that the two texts were closely related.", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "10'", "atf": "<{d}>e ša i-šu-u₂ i-lu ṭe-ma", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: (Then) (W)e, the god who took the initiative,"}, {"number": "11'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n pâšu | <ī>pušam-ma || ana ilī | [i]zzaqqar", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["o"], "number": "11'", "atf": "pa#-a-šu# <i>-pu-ša!-[m]a ana DINGIR#-MEŠ [i]z-za-qar\n$ end of side", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Opened his mouth and addressed the gods:"}, {"number": "12'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n i nimhaṣ-ma | guzalâ | labī<rū>ti", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "1", "atf": "i# ni#-im-ha-aṣ-ma {giš}GU.ZA.LA₂?# la?#-bi-<ru>-ti", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Let us smite the steward of old time,"}, {"number": "13'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... | išakkan | ellil", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "2", "atf": "[i?-š]u-tu?# x (x) x i-ša-ka!-an <{d}>en-lil₂", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Enlil will appoint …"}, {"number": "14'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] | išakkan", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "3", "atf": "i#-šu-x [(x)] x i-ša-ka-an <<nu>>", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: … […] will appoint"}, {"number": "15'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ... | ina mahrīni | ila | lemna?", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "4", "atf": "NE?# x [x] x i#-na mah#-ri-ni DINGIR lem?#-na", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: … in front of us … the @i{evil god},"}, {"number": "16'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... || unninī | alkāni", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "5", "atf": "x x x x-mu-u un-ni-ni al-ka-ni", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: … @i{will hear my} plea. Come,"}, {"number": "17'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... | [n]išebbira | nīrni\n#note: Compare line 8’ above: @i{u kabta dullāni i nišbir nīr}[@i{ni}] (see @bib{marquezrowe2016middle@64}, who reads @akk{al?#-ka?#-<ni?> [i? n]u?-šal-bi-ra}).", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "6", "atf": "x x (x) [n]i*-ši*-bi-ra ni-ir-ni", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: … we shall break our yoke,"}, {"number": "18'a", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n u kabta | dullani | nušassak | [e]lni!", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "7-8a", "atf": "u₃# ka#-ab-ta dul#-la#-ni nu-ša!#-an-sa*#-ak?# | [e]l*#-ni <<iš>>\n#note: @bib{RN59aa@173-74} interpret @akk{x-ni-iš} at the end of the line as the end of an adverbial form, absent from the OB and SB versions.\n$ line continues", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: and we shall take off (this) our heavy burden upon us."}, {"number": "18'b", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n mālik (|) ilī | qurā[da]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "8b", "atf": "ma-lik DINGIR-MEŠ qu₂#-ra#-[da]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: The counselor of the gods, the hero,"}, {"number": "19'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n alkāni | i niš[ši]ʾaššu | ina šu[b]t[īšu]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "9", "atf": "al-ka-ni i ni-iš-[ši]-a#-šu# i-na šu[b]-t[i-šu]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Come, let us fetch him from [his] dwelling!"}, {"number": "20'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ellil | mālik (|) ilī | qu[rāda]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "10", "atf": "{d}en-lil₂ ma-lik# DINGIR#-MEŠ# qu₂#-[ra-da]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Enlil, the counsellor of the gods, the hero,"}, {"number": "21'a", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [alkāni | i niššiʾaššu | ina šubtīšu]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "11a", "atf": "KI.MIN\n$ line continues", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: @i{Come, let us fetch him from his dwelling!}"}, {"number": "21'b", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n il[ū | išmû | zikiršu]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "11b", "atf": "DINGIR-ME[Š x x x x x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: The gods [@i{heard what he said}]."}, {"number": "22'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n u tupš[ikkīšunu | girra | ittakšū]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "12", "atf": "u₃# tup-ši-i[k-ki-šu-nu x x x x x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: [They put fire to their work] baskets."}, {"number": "23'", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 12, "labels": ["r"], "number": "13", "atf": "x x [x x x x x x x x x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: …"}], "record": {"authors": [], "translators": [], "publicationDate": ""}, "parserVersion": "6.1.0", "isFilteredQuery": false, "colophonLinesInQuery": {}}